// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Ivo Madsen: galley hand, late team, Bunk 2 berth 1. Off Monday and Tuesday.
// Roster: stubborn, chatty; garden-lover, shopper. Can carry six trays at once. Sings in the shower (the dawn chorus);
// presses flowers from the garden (Cruz pretends not to notice). No pronouns in facts.md: "Ivo" or "they".
//
// HOW THEY TALK: never stops, never unkind. Tells every story from the beginning. "Right, listen." Laughs at the joke
// before the end. Stubborn about small things: the right way to stack bowls, which side of a tray is the front.
// WITH JUNIORS: adopts you. Tells you everything about everyone (nothing secret, just a lot).
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: trays, flowers, who's in the garden, the store's new stock.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = sings (not only in the shower, which is worse). Low = quiet, which everyone notices at once.
// NEVER: wins an argument with Brennan; admits to the singing to your face (goes red, stops for a week).
// RUNNING: six trays, training for seven; argues with Brennan about bowls every day and has never won.
